{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960681,"nonce":"brVZTdeq8SR3dOqjmV6cd2OZ9OQ=","title":"replace rayzor-window with an adapter over xwindow","message":"`rayzor/window` is a hand-written Cocoa/X11/Win32 binding, behind the window libraries the other runtimes get. xwindow (github.com/rayzor-blade/xwindow) generates the same `window` API for Caribou, Ash and Rayzor from one declaration, over winit natively and the page's canvas in a browser. A Rayzor window package built on it closes the gap, as rayzor-gpu did over xgpu.\n\nThe adapter, as a scratch build proved:\n\n- a cdylib with `rayzor_plugin::export_abi_version!()` and `rpkg_entry!(XIDL_METHODS, xidl_runtime_symbols)`;\n- `xwindow_bindgen::generate(Runtime::Rayzor)` included at the crate root, `xwindow_backend::install` for `mod backend`, and `crate::runtime` carriers like rayzor-gpu's `xgpu_runtime.rs`;\n- the Haxe tree from `xwindow-haxe rayzor`, package `window`; symbols are `xwindow_*` and classes `window::*`, so the method table and the externs agree.\n\nPacked into an rpkg, the scratch adapter opens a window under the JIT, reports its platform, size, scale and monitor, and polls events, once native constructors bind (7920361d50f3dedb25b6cf5210df49b9834d7bfa568bd176076c6f0da98c3b93, fixed). Text results still crash (518bcb82076962f5678dc7f5feb3d09eabfcce821d851b8a12395ad9c674a62e).\n\nWhat the replacement retires in the current crate:\n\n- it never calls `export_abi_version!()`, so `check_plugin_abi` refuses it on both the rpkg and `--native-lib` paths;\n- `rayzor_window_run_loop` takes `extern \"C\" fn() -\u003e i32`, while Haxe passes `runLoop(win, callback:Dynamic)` a closure record (from reading; not run);\n- `examples/gpu-window/Main.hx` imports `rayzor.gpu` classes that no longer exist.","files":null}]}